  "description": "I still have a soft spot for cold peanut noodles. These days, I make them with far fewer noodles and many more vegetables. Indeed, it's now more of a vegetable salad with a few noodles added in for textural contrast. A handful of fresh herbs rounds out the flavors.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: 1 to 2 red Thai bird chiles, finely minced (optional)\n\nOptional substitutions: sugar → honey; red bell peppers → orange bell peppers or yellow bell peppers\n\nNotes: Fresh Chinese wheat noodles are available in most Asian markets. 1/4 pound dried linguini, fettuccini, or spaghetti can be substituted if fresh Chinese noodles are unavailable.",
